Whats a router?
    - Forwards traffic between subnets, between an internal and external network, or between two external networks

How PC1 communicates to PC2 through a network
    1.  Two routers will have some kind of connectivity between eachother
    2.  PC1 sends an ARP packet to switch which will realize it does not know the MAC address to the destination device within that local area.
    3.  That ARP Request gets forwarded to the default gateway of the router 1
    4.  The router 1 then sends a ARP reply to PC1
    5.  PC1 sends data frame to the router 1 where the MAC address is then switched to an IP address
    6.  Router 1 packs it into a layer 3 packet and then adds an IP header to it.
    7.  The data is now able to go across to another router.
    8.  Router 1 sends that data to router 2.
    9.  Router 2 recives the data and strips the IP header off of the packet and brings it back down to layer 2 frames
    10. Router correlates PC2's MAC address with the destination IP of the packet
    11. Since they are on the same network, the switch takes the information from the router 2 and directs it to PC2